.Dd July 25, 2026
.Dt MAC_CAPABILITY 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac_capability
.Nd Capability Message Interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load at boot (required for program nonce):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo 'mac_capability_load="YES"' >> /boot/loader.conf
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a message-passing capability framework for kernel modules.
Capabilities are represented as file descriptors of type
.Dv DTYPE_MAC_CAPABILITY .
Each capability is an instance of a kernel service, accessed through
structured ioctls.
.Pp
The
.Pa /dev/mac_capability
device is normally claimed exclusively by
.Xr authorityd 8
at boot via the isolation service.
Once claimed, only
.Xr authorityd 8
can open the device; all other processes receive
.Er EACCES .
Administrative access to capability services is provided through
.Xr authorityctl 8 .
.Pp
The framework supports two messaging models:
.Bl -tag -width "Synchronous"
.It Sy Asynchronous
Messages are enqueued via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG
and async replies or notifications are dequeued via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG .
The service processes messages on a kernel taskqueue.
.It Sy Synchronous
Requests are made via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL .
The service handler runs in the caller's thread context.
.El
.Pp
A service may expose asynchronous messaging, synchronous calls, or both.
Services that do not accept
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG
may still emit asynchronous notifications on
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG .
.Xr kqueue 2
readiness maps to the async queues:
.Dv EVFILT_READ
means
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG
can make progress, and
.Dv EVFILT_WRITE
means space is available for
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG .
Service-defined events are delivered as
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG
payloads; kqueue notes provide readiness, not the event payload itself.
.Pp
The device node
.Pa /dev/mac_capability
is created at module load with mode 0600 (root only).
.Ss Creating a capability
Open
.Pa /dev/mac_capability
and issue
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CONNECT
with the name of the desired service.
On success, a new capability file descriptor is returned in the
.Va fd
field.
The
.Pa /dev/mac_capability
descriptor can then be closed.
.Ss Credential trailer
Every message carries a kernel-stamped credential trailer containing
the sender's uid, gid, jail ID, and program nonce.
The nonce is an 8-byte cryptographic random value that identifies the
program image: it is inherited across
.Xr fork 2
and rotated on
.Xr execve 2 .
Zero is never a valid nonce.
.Ss Capability control
.Bl -tag -width MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_MINT
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_SEND
Strip the ability to send async messages.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_RECV
Strip the ability to receive async messages.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_CALL
Strip the ability to make synchronous calls.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_MINT
Strip the ability to mint new instances.
One-way latch.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_TERMINATE
Kill the instance for all holders.
Subsequent operations return
.Er ECONNRESET .
.El
.Ss Minting
Services created with the
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SVC_MINTABLE
flag allow holders to create new instances via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MINT_INSTANCE .
The mint ability can be removed with
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_MINT .
.Ss Introspection
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_GETINFO
returns the service name, badge, queue limits, and feature flags
.Pq Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_INFO_F_SENDMSG , MAC_CAPABILITY_INFO_F_RECVMSG , MAC_CAPABILITY_INFO_F_CALL , MAC_CAPABILITY_INFO_F_KQUEUE .
Standard file-descriptor tools such as
.Xr procstat 1
show
.Nm
descriptors as
.Dq mac_capability:service[badge] .
The path may include compact state suffixes such as
.Dq :no-send ,
.Dq :no-recv ,
.Dq :no-call ,
.Dq :no-mint ,
.Dq :revoked ,
and
.Dq :closed .
.Ss File descriptor passing
Capabilities can carry up to 32 file descriptors per message.
Attached fds preserve their Capsicum rights and ioctl allowlists through the
transfer.
The sender may impose a narrower transfer ceiling with
.Xr cap_xfer_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_xfer_ioctls_limit 2 ,
and
.Xr cap_xfer_fcntls_limit 2 ;
the receiver obtains the intersection while the sender remains unchanged.
.Ss Capsicum integration
.Nm
descriptors participate in
.Xr capsicum 4
rights enforcement.
The
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
right permits ioctl use on a descriptor, while
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2
irreversibly restricts the descriptor to a command allowlist.
For example, a send-only capability retains
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
and allowlists
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG .
.Pp
Introspection and narrowing commands are not exempt from Capsicum checks.
They require
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
and must remain in the descriptor's ioctl allowlist if the list is limited:
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_GETINFO ,
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_SEND ,
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_RECV ,
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_CALL ,
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_MINT ,
and
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_TERMINATE .
.Ss Service creation flags
Kernel modules register services with the following optional flags:
.Bl -tag -width MAC_CAPABILITY_SVC_MINTABLE
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SVC_NOTIFY Pq 0x0002
Service emits async notifications.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SVC_MINTABLE Pq 0x0004
Instances can mint new instances via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MINT_INSTANCE .
.El
.Sh IOCTLS
.Bl -tag -width MAC_CAPABILITY_MINT_INSTANCE
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CONNECT
Connect to a named service.
Returns a capability fd.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG
Send an async message with optional fd attachment.
Returns
.Er EAGAIN
if the RX queue is full; wait for
.Dv EVFILT_WRITE
and retry.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG
Receive an async message.
Blocks unless
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
is set.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL
Synchronous request/reply in the caller's thread.
Returns
.Er EMSGSIZE
with the required size if the reply buffer is too small.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_GETINFO
Query capability metadata: service name, badge, queue limits, and
feature flags.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_SEND
Strip send ability.
One-way latch.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_RECV
Strip receive ability.
One-way latch.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_CALL
Strip call ability.
One-way latch.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_MINT
Strip mint ability.
One-way latch.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_TERMINATE
Kill the instance for all holders.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MINT_INSTANCE
Create a new instance from an existing mintable instance.
Requires
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
and an ioctl allowlist containing
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MINT_INSTANCE .
Only available on services registered with the
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SVC_MINTABLE
flag.
.El
.Sh SERVICES
The following services are provided as loadable kernel modules:
.Bl -tag -width mac_capability_capprotect
.It Sy mac_capability_identity
Program nonce queries.
Provides SELF and QUERY operations via
.Xr procdesc 4 .
See
.Xr mac_capability_identity 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_capprotect
Capability protection via MACF.
Selectively shield a program from ptrace, signals, visibility,
and wait.
Same-nonce (fork family) processes interact freely;
foreign programs are blocked.
Provides shield, mint, authorize, capmode, and chroot operations.
See
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_isolation
File, network, vsock, and jail isolation by nonce.
Supports claims, tokens, and MACF enforcement.
.Pp
Vsock endpoint claims may cover bind or connect operations for a CID and
32-bit port range.
A provider claim covers the complete port range of one concrete guest CID and
authorizes attachment and subsequent access to that CID's
.Pa /dev/vsock
host-transport descriptor.
An endpoint claim does not grant provider authority.
Multiple provider descriptors may coexist when their guest CIDs differ;
duplicate CID attachment is rejected.
.Pp
Provider authority follows the descriptor, but remains scoped to the program
nonce that owned the claim at attachment.
After descriptor passing or
.Xr execve 2 ,
a foreign nonce needs a matching authorization token.
Closing the original claim does not make an attached protected provider
public, and a provider attached before a claim is created honors that later
claim.
See
.Xr mac_capability_isolation 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_system
System operation gating via MACF.
Controls kldload, reboot, sysctl, and other privileged operations.
See
.Xr mac_capability_system 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_coalition
Resource group management.
Provides enlist, terminate, deadline, watchdog, and related operations.
See
.Xr mac_capability_coalition 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_node
Per-process inspection and control via
.Xr procdesc 4 .
See
.Xr mac_capability_node 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_accounting
Per-process racct/rctl operations via
.Xr procdesc 4 .
See
.Xr mac_capability_accounting 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_channel
Bidirectional capability channel for peer-to-peer messaging.
See
.Xr mac_capability_channel 4 .
.It Sy mac_capability_mount
Capability-based filesystem mounting.
See
.Xr mac_capability_mount 4 .
.El
.Ss Test fixtures
The following services exist for testing the MAC_CAPABILITY framework.
They are not intended for production use.
.Bl -tag -width mac_capability_test_kernelstore
.It Sy mac_capability_test_kernelstore
Sync-only shared key-value store (256 keys, 4096 bytes per value).
.It Sy mac_capability_test_keystore
Async key-value store.
.El
.Sh AUTHORITY MODEL
Authority in the capability plane is a
.Em held capability ,
never an identity.
A capability is a channel endpoint bound to an
.Pq Do object , rights Dc
pair: the descriptor is the credential, holding it is holding the authority,
and using it is presenting the capability.
A service acts on a request because of which endpoint it arrived on and the
rights that endpoint carries \(em it does not consult the caller's uid, gid,
pathname, or process id to authorize.
.Pp
Four operations define the model.
.Bl -tag -width delegate
.It Sy present
Send a request on the endpoint; the service honors it if the endpoint's rights
permit the operation.
.It Sy delegate
Hand the endpoint to another holder by passing the descriptor; whether it may be
re-delegated is an attenuable property of the descriptor
.Pq see Xr cap_xfer_rights_limit 2 .
.It Sy attenuate
Mint a strictly weaker capability \(em fewer rights, or a narrower object \(em
from one already held; attenuation is one-way.
.It Sy revoke
Invalidate a capability and, transitively, everything minted from it.
.El
.Pp
Identity becomes capability at exactly one boundary: the kernel mints
unforgeable endpoints, PID\ 1
.Pq Xr authorityd 8
holds the root capability at boot, and an authentication agent exchanges a
proven credential for that principal's capability bundle by explicit policy.
Above that boundary no component derives authority from a uid; uids name
principals and protect the POSIX substrate only.
This is the target model that new code is written to; the phased migration of
existing authorization onto it, and the locked design decisions, are recorded in
.Pa /usr/src/docs/capability-authority-model.md .
.Sh LIMITS
.Bl -tag -width MAC_CAPABILITY_MSG_PAYLOAD_SIZE
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MSG_PAYLOAD_SIZE
14336 bytes (14 KB) maximum usable payload per message.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MAX_FDS
32 file descriptors per message.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MAXNAME
64 bytes maximum service name length.
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_DEFAULT_QUEUE_DEPTH
256 messages per async queue (configurable by service).
.It Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH
4096 messages maximum async queue depth.
.El
.Pp
Messages are fixed at 16384 bytes (4 pages) including a 2048-byte
header reserved for framework use.
Sync-only services do not allocate message queues.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width kern.mac_capability.service_details
.It Va kern.mac_capability.services
Number of registered services.
.It Va kern.mac_capability.instances
Number of active capability instances.
.It Va kern.mac_capability.service_names
Newline-separated list of registered service names.
.It Va kern.mac_capability.service_details
Newline-separated list of registered services with flags, queue depth,
TX limit, instance limit, active instance count, and destroying state.
.El
.Sh DTRACE PROBES
The
.Nm
provider defines the following probes.
.Ss Core messaging
connect, connect-done, send, send-done, recv, recv-done, dispatch,
dispatch-done, reply, reply-done, notify, notify-done, call, call-done,
forward, forward-done, revoke, revoke-done, close.
.Ss FD lifecycle
fd-install, fd-close, fd-receive, fd-mint.
.Ss Control
control, ioctl-deny, rights-change, state, error.
.Ss Instance lifecycle
instance-create, instance-finalize, instance-lastclose.
.Ss Service lifecycle
service-create, service-destroy.
.Ss Queue
queue-pressure.
.Pp
The descriptor probes include the service name, badge, fd, pid,
credential pointer, and nonce.
The control probe includes the service name, badge, ioctl command, pid,
credential pointer, and nonce.
The state probe passes service name, badge, instance flags, restriction
bits, pid, and nonce so scripts do not have to infer descriptor state
from prior events.
These probes cover descriptor events visible to
.Nm
itself; generic
.Xr dup 2 ,
fork inheritance, and
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
transfer through Unix sockets require fd-layer instrumentation.
.Pp
Related providers include
.Va fd
for descriptor install, dup, close, fork inheritance,
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
send/receive, and pass-deny events;
.Va capsicum
for rights/ioctl/fcntl limit, get, check, and denial events;
.Va mac_capability_nonce
for nonce assign, copy, backfill, and exec-rotate events;
and subsystem providers
.Va mac_capability_capprotect ,
.Va mac_capability_isolation ,
.Va mac_capability_system ,
.Va mac_capability_coalition ,
and
.Va mac_capability_channel
for claim, token, authorization, release, and denial events.
.Pp
Installed DTrace scripts for observing
.Nm
and related descriptor authority include:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width mac_capability-coalitions -compact
.It Pa mac_capability-audit
Comprehensive audit trail of all
.Nm
operations.
.It Pa mac_capability-calls
Synchronous call latency and frequency.
.It Pa mac_capability-coalitions
Coalition membership and lifecycle events.
.It Pa mac_capability-delegation
Capability delegation through fd passing.
.It Pa mac_capability-denials
Denied operations from MACF and Capsicum.
.It Pa mac_capability-errors
Error frequency by service and error code.
.It Pa mac_capability-fds
File descriptor lifecycle for
.Nm
descriptors.
.It Pa mac_capability-holders
Active capability holders by service.
.It Pa mac_capability-messages
Async message throughput and queue depth.
.It Pa mac_capability-nonces
Program nonce assignment and rotation.
.It Pa mac_capability-services
Service registration and instance counts.
.It Pa mac_capability-shield
capprotect shield and authorization events.
.It Pa mac_capability-summary
Aggregate statistics across all services.
.It Pa mac_capability-who
Per-process capability usage summary.
.It Pa capsicum-changes
Capsicum rights changes across all descriptor types.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/mac_capability
.It Pa /dev/mac_capability
Control device for creating capabilities.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
RX queue full
.Pq Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG ,
no message available with
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
.Pq Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG ,
or TX soft limit reached for notifications.
.It Bq Er EACCES
Operation revoked via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_* ,
Capsicum rights check failed, or restriction flag triggered.
.It Bq Er EBADF
File descriptor hold failed during message construction.
.It Bq Er ECONNABORTED
Service being destroyed during
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CONNECT .
.It Bq Er ECONNRESET
Instance terminated or peer closed.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
Invalid arguments, reserved fields nonzero, payload too large, or
too many file descriptors attached.
.It Bq Er EMSGSIZE
Payload too large
.Pq Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG ,
or reply buffer too small
.Pq Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG , MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL .
The required size is returned in the length field.
.It Bq Er ENOBUFS
TX hard limit reached
.Pq queue_depth * 4 .
.It Bq Er ENOENT
Service not found
.Pq Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CONNECT .
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
Wrong messaging model for this service:
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG
on a sync-only service,
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL
on an async-only service, or
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_MINT_INSTANCE
on a non-mintable service.
.It Bq Er EPIPE
Instance dead on
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Connect to a service and make a synchronous call:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int devfd, capfd;
struct mac_capability_connect_args conn;
struct mac_capability_call_args call;
char req[128], reply[1024];

devfd = open("/dev/mac_capability", O_RDWR);

memset(&conn, 0, sizeof(conn));
strlcpy(conn.name, "mac_capability_identity", sizeof(conn.name));
if (ioctl(devfd, MAC_CAPABILITY_CONNECT, &conn) == -1)
	err(1, "connect");
capfd = conn.fd;
close(devfd);

memset(&call, 0, sizeof(call));
call.tx_data = req;
call.tx_len = sizeof(req);
call.rx_data = reply;
call.rx_len = sizeof(reply);
if (ioctl(capfd, MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL, &call) == -1)
	err(1, "call");

/* call.rx_len now contains the actual reply size */
.Ed
.Pp
Narrow a capability for delegation to an untrusted child:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/* Strip send and mint, keep only recv and call */
ioctl(capfd, MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_SEND, NULL);
ioctl(capfd, MAC_CAPABILITY_REVOKE_MINT, NULL);
cap_xfer_limit(capfd, CAP_XFER_NONE);  /* prevent further delegation */
.Ed
.Pp
Poll for async messages with
.Xr kqueue 2 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct kevent ev;
EV_SET(&ev, capfd, EVFILT_READ, EV_ADD, 0, 0, NULL);
kevent(kq, &ev, 1, NULL, 0, NULL);

/* In event loop */
if (kevent(kq, NULL, 0, &ev, 1, NULL) > 0) {
	struct mac_capability_recvmsg_args rmsg;
	memset(&rmsg, 0, sizeof(rmsg));
	rmsg.rx_data = buf;
	rmsg.rx_len = sizeof(buf);
	ioctl(capfd, MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG, &rmsg);
}
.Ed
